WEBVTT

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.920
To You Clowns

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:14.630
Hey, you!

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.090
When are you taking off
those ugly masks?

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:20.420
It’s just that you don’t
have the courage to.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.510
Coating your insubstantial true
identity with your pretensions.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:26.430
You’re just waiting for me
to fall into your trap, right?

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:27.930
Sorry to burst your bubble!

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:30.310
I’m not dumb enough to fall for that.

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:32.690
Enough with this ludicrous act.

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:34.980
If you stop, then I’ll dance with you.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.360
A dancing fool and a fool who watches!

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.400
Hey, dancing tonight!

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:43.780
Hey, you! What are you doing,
reading my stuff like that?

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:46.450
I've told you a thousand
times not to read my stuff!

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.080
Moron! I-It's not
what you think, okay?

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.870
We're so not dancing tonight, okay?

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:57.040
W-W-Why don't you go off
and dance by yourself?

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:46.820
Who is that guy?

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:50.200
Today, the teacher asked us what
we wanted to be when we grew up!

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.990
Risette was adorable!

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:53.740
Oh, really? What do you
want to be, Jun-kun?

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:53.740
Yeah, they were all awesome!

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.700
Maybe I'll start a band, too!

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:16.890
<i>Today, we'll be hearing from
full-time farmer, Mr. Shibasaki.</i>

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:18.270
<i>Hello.</i>

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:19.440
<i>Hello!</i>

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.810
<i>Wow! Just look at this!</i>

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:24.400
<i>It looks delicious.
May I have a taste?</i>

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:25.900
<i>Please do.</i>

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.190
<i>All right, I'm going to try one.</i>

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:32.410
<i>Oh, yes! They're so juicy!</i>

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:35.540
<i>Aren't they? What do you say?</i>

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:40.620
<i>If you married my son, you could have
all the fresh veggies you wanted!</i>

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.160
Jeez, I'm going, okay?

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:44.040
<i>This is Yamano, reporting
from Mr. Shibasaki's farm.</i>

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:55.560
Just go straight down
this street. It's not far.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:58.560
It's exactly the hick town
I was told it would be.

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:02.100
With a low crime rate, too.

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.820
Inaba Police Station

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:08.820
Five minutes late on your first day?

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:10.700
You've got some guts.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:18.120
This may be a little town in the sticks,
but that attitude's not going to cut it.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:20.500
Right, sorry about that.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:23.710
If you have five minutes,
you can canvas for two incidents.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.920
One of those guys
who never get ahead...

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:24.790
Don't forget...

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.250
Who lives and dies
by working it in the field...

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:29.550
In the field, every minute,
every second counts.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:30.380
An old-school cop whose
motto is "Pound the pavement..."

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:30.380
Right...

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:33.130
The type I don't get along with.

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:37.390
She's already gone to bed
tonight, but I've got a daughter.

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:38.890
Her name's Nanako.

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:40.520
She's nothing like me.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:41.640
A real good kid.

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:49.730
I hear that you went through a lot
in the city, but this is a tiny hick town.

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:53.660
Helping each other out really
strengthens people's bonds.

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:57.990
You're free to consider this
place your own home.

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:00.450
I look forward to working with you.

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:01.830
Right!

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:04.460
I look forward to
working with you, too.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:10.800
Oh, man! So good!

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:48.840
Uh, about that purse-snatching
case the other day...

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:53.720
It was in front of the... Four-Six...

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:54.880
The Shiroku shop.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:06:00.510
Right, the culprit snatched the purse
in front of the Shiroku shop, and fled by bicycle.

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:03.600
That was when...
at Point A, Ai...?

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:04.850
Aiya.

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:09.150
Right, right! He passed
Aiya's delivery girl,

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:11.780
and apparently she saw his face.

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:16.240
Since both incidents occurred in
the Inaba International Shopping District...

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:18.490
That's "Central Shopping District."

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:20.740
Oh, that's right!

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:23.750
Oh, boy...

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.500
A month after I came to this town...

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:35.300
Rumors started flying
about the Midnight Channel,

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:39.260
which would show your
soul mate on TV at midnight.

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:47.850
<i>Today, we have a special guest - Mongolian,
the genius dog who has everyone talking!</i>

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:54.030
<i>And can you believe it, Mongolian is a very special dog
who can walk across a tightrope on his hind legs!</i>

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:55.900
<i>What an amazing skill!</i>

00:06:55.900 --> 00:07:00.160
<i>Yes, I don't think any other
dog can do what mine can.</i>

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.160
<i>How incredible is that?</i>

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:06.580
<i>Yes, I believe he's been
blessed with talent.</i>

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:28.480
No way...

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.150
You gotta be kidding me.

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:10.850
What the hell is this?

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:14.940
This is crazy.

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:17.860
It's totally crazy!

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:26.790
Just when it was getting interesting.

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:29.370
You really are clueless, Dojima-san.

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:34.380
For some reason...

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:42.630
The newscaster, Mayumi
Yamano. You know her?

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:44.300
The one having the affair.

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:45.300
Affair?

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:51.690
Popular Female Anchor

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:51.690
SECRET
MEETING

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:49.180
This Ms. Yamano is
here in Inaba City.

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:51.690
She's staying at
the Amagi Inn right now.

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:56.440
But the media got wind of it
and they're mobbing the inn.

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:59.190
I hear it's turned into
something of an uproar.

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:03.030
So the department's been
asked to provide security.

00:09:03.030 --> 00:09:06.200
Can you join the detail
starting tomorrow?

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:07.370
Hey...

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:08.990
Y-Yes.

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:11.750
Uh, what about Dojima-san?

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:13.460
Didn't he tell you?

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:16.000
He's taking time off
for family reasons.

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:22.170
Whereabouts? That way?

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:24.510
Pounding the pavement
to investigate...

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:27.300
Something I never knew
how to do till I came to this town.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.390
I told you, I'm not answering
anything unless it's about art!

00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:30.850
Right...

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:33.770
Pretty tough...

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:38.360
Souzai Daigaku's steak skewers, huh?
I'll keep these in mind.

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:49.080
That weird lady's shop is the Shiroku,
and that shady-looking one is Daidara.

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:52.000
There's the Marukyu Tofu
Shop, and that's Aiya.

00:09:53.870 --> 00:09:56.500
Who gives a damn about all this?

00:09:57.750 --> 00:09:59.340
Uh, Dojima-san?

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:03.210
Hey, if you're gonna take
the day off, at least tell me!

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:04.630
<i>But I did tell you.</i>

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:06.800
Huh? Did you?

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:08.510
Well, never mind.

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:12.890
I've been canvassing the shopping
district, but it's a dead end.

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:14.640
No new information to be had...

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:15.730
<i>Is that right?</i>

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:18.520
It's so old-school,
your way of doing things.

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:22.190
<i>Sorry, Adachi. If it's not an emergency,
can we pick this up later?</i>

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:24.440
<i>I'm out shopping right now.</i>

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:25.490
Shopping?

00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:29.990
Starting on Monday, my nephew's
 staying with me for a year.

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:32.450
So I'm out getting stuff
that he might need.

00:10:32.450 --> 00:10:34.700
Daddy, what about a toothbrush?

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:36.370
Whoops, that too!

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:39.830
Oh, yeah? Your nephew, huh?

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:43.960
<i>So anyway, sorry about that.
I'll call you back later.</i>

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:58.140
This story that you're
having an affair...

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:00.230
It's a lie, right? A story like that...

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:01.770
It's none of your business!

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:04.070
Not denying it, huh?

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:06.900
After I was nice to you...

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:10.530
Who knew you were
such a piece of trash?

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:13.950
I-I'm going to call somebody!

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:18.540
Shut up! Shut up!
Shut up! Shut the hell up!

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:21.880
You know what?

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:26.050
You need a good scare, and
get yourself straightened out...

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:30.550
For example...

00:11:44.110 --> 00:11:45.940
She fell in.

00:11:48.860 --> 00:11:50.570
That's amazing...

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:53.240
You can go all the way in!

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:52.590
Look, you, you've been fooling around
with Namatame, haven't you?

00:12:52.590 --> 00:12:53.970
Stay away from me!

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:56.430
So why not do the same with me?

00:12:56.430 --> 00:12:57.560
Stop it!

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:01.560
I wonder why...

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:07.570
Why is that I...

00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:11.320
I'm not good enough?

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:12.570
Ryotaro Dojima

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:19.200
Ryotaro Dojima

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:22.460
Ryotaro Dojima

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:25.960
Ryotaro Dojima

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:29.590
Ryotaro Dojima

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:30.840
One Voice Message

00:13:34.050 --> 00:13:36.340
High school girl, yeah right!

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:38.850
This whole world is crap.

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:43.180
Cry and beg for forgiveness!
Then I'll let you out!

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:44.980
Just kidding...

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:02.040
<i>Adachi, where are you now?</i>

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:07.920
<i>It's nothing urgent, but I was wondering
if you'd like to come to dinner tonight.</i>

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:10.380
<i>If you're up to it, call me back.</i>

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:30.480
He's gone...

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:31.320
Marie!

00:14:31.940 --> 00:14:33.320
What's going on?

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:35.070
Everyone's worried about you.

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:38.820
That's Adachi-san.

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:41.280
He works under Dojima-san,
 and he's a cop.

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:43.160
I invited him to the concert.

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:44.620
Adachi...

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:46.920
Why were you chasing Adachi-san?

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:48.630
I don't know...

00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:50.090
But...

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:54.800
You should stay away from that man.

00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:55.590
Why?

00:14:55.970 --> 00:15:00.390
I don't know. I don't know why,
but that's the vibe I'm getting.

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:02.390
That complicates things.

00:15:02.390 --> 00:15:04.970
Is he... your friend?

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:08.980
I'm not sure. I guess I just
want to know more about him.

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:27.580
Now that I think of it, that day
might have started the ball rolling.

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:30.420
Which one should I choose?

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:33.340
Nanako-chan, how about
growing cabbages?

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:35.050
I really love them.

00:15:35.050 --> 00:15:36.090
Cabbage?

00:15:36.090 --> 00:15:38.130
Oh, wait, you don't like them?

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:39.760
What do you want, Big Bro?

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:43.720
Anything you like, Nanako.

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:45.520
Big Bro, huh?

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:48.020
You've totally warmed up to him.

00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:49.890
Tohru-chan!

00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:53.110
What are you doing here?

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:55.030
Are you done with work?

00:15:56.900 --> 00:16:00.530
Oh, well, I'm off today. Um...

00:16:00.530 --> 00:16:01.450
Hello!

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:02.280
Hello.

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:04.660
Oh, hello there.

00:16:04.660 --> 00:16:09.540
Are you friends of Tohru-chan's?
You're so young to be his friends.

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:12.500
That's right, they're friends of mine.

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:14.920
We're shopping now, and really busy...

00:16:14.920 --> 00:16:20.760
Oh, is that right? Then I'll bring you
some stew again sometime, all right?

00:16:20.760 --> 00:16:23.800
You have to take care of yourself.

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:25.430
See you later!

00:16:25.430 --> 00:16:26.560
Goodbye!

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:31.190
That lady's son has
the same name as me, see.

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:35.070
Apparently, he looks like me, too,
so she's really been doting on me.

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:36.780
You seem pretty happy about that.

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:38.530
Are you kidding?

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:41.200
It's actually a nuisance, you know.

00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:45.830
Bringing over tons of stew,
when I never asked for it...

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:49.830
I really wish she'd back off!

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:55.960
Come to think of it,
I never returned it.

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:05.680
Adachi-san?

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:09.680
What are you doing here?

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:12.230
I'm ditching work.

00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:14.190
Don't tell Dojima-san, okay?

00:17:14.190 --> 00:17:15.690
Tohru-chan!

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:17.070
Oh, crap.

00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:19.940
This really blows.

00:17:19.940 --> 00:17:22.450
I've had it with her stew.

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:22.450
Over here!

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:25.570
Wait up, Mom.

00:17:26.530 --> 00:17:27.740
Well, well!

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:30.250
Mr. Detective and his friends?

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:31.200
Hello.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:32.330
Hello...

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:36.290
Let me introduce you.
This is my son, Tohru-chan.

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:37.960
Hello, nice to meet you.

00:17:37.960 --> 00:17:46.050
My Tohru-chan's so busy with work, but
he's here just to see me, and I'm so happy!

00:17:46.050 --> 00:17:49.470
I'm going to make you lots
and lots of stew tonight!

00:17:49.470 --> 00:17:51.730
That sounds great, Mom.

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:55.480
Have a good day, Mr. Detective.

00:17:57.940 --> 00:18:01.990
So it doesn't have to
be me after all, huh?

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:06.110
I mean, just how do we
resemble each other?

00:18:06.110 --> 00:18:07.990
He doesn't look a thing like me.

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:12.500
It's a little sad, isn't it?

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:15.250
Why?

00:18:23.050 --> 00:18:24.010
Hello.

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:25.630
You...

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:27.010
What's going on?

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:29.260
I thought I'd bring you...

00:18:29.550 --> 00:18:30.890
This.

00:18:32.140 --> 00:18:34.350
Hey, hold on...

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:36.020
Please eat this.

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:41.150
The smaller one is a single meal, so
please warm it up whenever you want.

00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:42.780
But why?

00:18:43.150 --> 00:18:44.740
For some reason...

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:46.660
Can we leave it at that?

00:18:47.030 --> 00:18:49.030
Oh, I see.

00:18:53.870 --> 00:18:55.120
Adachi-san?

00:18:55.710 --> 00:18:58.710
Would you like to come
over for dinner tonight?

00:18:58.710 --> 00:18:59.880
Today?

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:02.800
I'm sure that both Dojima-san
and Nanako would be thrilled.

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:06.590
I made you a boxed lunch
from today's leftovers.

00:19:06.590 --> 00:19:08.550
Please have it by tomorrow.

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:11.550
You're waiting on me
hand and foot, huh?

00:19:11.550 --> 00:19:14.350
How much should I pay you?

00:19:14.350 --> 00:19:16.270
I don't need any payment.

00:19:16.270 --> 00:19:18.560
Because I'm just
doing this on my own.

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:20.020
Yeah, but...

00:19:20.020 --> 00:19:22.520
What's in it for you, then?

00:19:22.520 --> 00:19:26.700
There's no profit or loss involved
when you're helping each other out.

00:19:34.450 --> 00:19:36.450
Helping each other out...

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:38.120
Right.

00:20:16.410 --> 00:20:18.540
"Stay away from me."

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:20.040
Uh-huh.

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:22.290
So why did you come anyway?

00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:26.630
I thought that Marie must have
her reasons for saying such a thing.

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:28.340
A reason, huh?

00:20:28.340 --> 00:20:29.880
I have no clue.

00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:32.300
I mean, this
Marie-chan... was it?

00:20:32.300 --> 00:20:34.100
Who is she?

00:20:34.350 --> 00:20:36.770
She doesn't seem to
go to your school...

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:38.020
She's a friend.

00:20:38.020 --> 00:20:40.310
Oh, so you can't tell me.

00:20:40.890 --> 00:20:43.560
I just can't ignore Marie, either.

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:46.610
And that's why you're
hanging with her?

00:20:47.190 --> 00:20:48.650
What's up with that?

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:53.450
Is it wrong to want to help
someone who's in trouble?

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:59.250
There's no way to know whether it's
wrong or not until you have results.

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:04.210
What you do for someone else
isn't always good for that person.

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:07.340
She could always betray you,

00:21:07.340 --> 00:21:10.720
and it might also lead
to something even worse.

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:14.180
If that's the case, then you just
shouldn't do anything from the start.

00:21:14.180 --> 00:21:17.350
That's how it works for grownups.

00:21:17.350 --> 00:21:18.470
But that...

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:21.230
That can't possibly be true.

00:21:34.610 --> 00:21:40.200
Someone must've done something
they shouldn't, and made the culprit mad.

00:21:35.780 --> 00:21:36.570
Crap!

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:37.620
Dammit!

00:21:37.870 --> 00:21:40.200
Damn, why Nanako-chan?

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:43.460
That's right...

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:46.460
This is all on you.

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:52.970
Playing crime avengers is what caused
Dojima-san and Nanako-chan's suffering...

00:21:54.180 --> 00:21:55.840
It was you.

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:03.600
This is all on you.

00:22:05.310 --> 00:22:06.730
Nanako!

00:22:07.610 --> 00:22:09.230
It was you.

00:22:15.070 --> 00:22:16.990
It was you, all right?

00:22:17.320 --> 00:22:18.330
Nanako.

00:22:18.330 --> 00:22:19.620
Nanako!

00:22:19.830 --> 00:22:22.700
Nanako!

00:22:40.430 --> 00:22:43.100
See? I told you...

00:22:43.640 --> 00:22:45.350
Yu-kun.

00:24:18.450 --> 00:24:20.200
I thought you'd be showing up soon.

00:24:20.200 --> 00:24:21.950
I'm going to stop you!

00:24:21.950 --> 00:24:24.660
There you go again, relying on it...

00:24:24.660 --> 00:24:26.700
The power of what you call a bond!

00:24:26.700 --> 00:24:28.830
So what if it is whitewashing?
